<title>INDIA: POLL-India IDBI 6-mth net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-India IDBI 6-mth net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Industrial Development Bank of India's (IDBI) net profit is forecast to rise 11.7 percent to 5.7 billion rupees in the first half of fiscal 1997/98, (April-March), a consensus Reuter poll showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>IDBI is India's largest term lending institution.</p>
<p>Its income is projected to rise 9.1 percent to 30.3 billion in the six months to September 30, 1997, according to 18 leading brokerages and securities houses.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>IDBI  ----PAT seen up 11.7%, income 9.1%</p>
<p>Average		5,741.56  5,140.00    30,281.58  27,760.00</p>
<p>High		   7,572.00		  35,952.00</p>
<p>Low		    5,557.00		  29,041.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk 91-22-265-9000</p>
